title: Flip only when asked
mode: draw
chapter: Memory
check: behaves
parts: dff chip:my_xor
needs: my_xor
---- intro
Your flip-flop that flips changes at **every** tick. Often you want it to flip only when a control `t` (toggle) is on, and keep its value otherwise:

| t | at the tick, q becomes |
|---|---|
| 0 | `q` (it stays) |
| 1 | NOT `q` (it flips) |

Look at the table: the new `q` is `q` XOR `t`. XOR with 0 changes nothing, XOR with 1 flips it.
---- task
Make `q` flip at a tick only while `t` is on, using a flip-flop and **my_xor**.
---- start
input t 0 0
clock clk 0 120
led q 440 40
---- reference
input t
clock clk
led q
wire w[1]
w = dff(w ^ t, clk)
q = w
---- answer
input t 0 0
clock clk 0 120
chip x1 my_xor 140 30
dff f1 280 40
led q 440 40
f1.q -> x1.a
t -> x1.b
x1.y -> f1.d
clk -> f1.clk
f1.q -> q
---- hint1
The flip-flop's `d` comes from my_xor.
---- hint2
my_xor gets the flip-flop's own `q` and `t`. The flip-flop's `q` also goes to the light.
---- solution
my_xor of `q` and `t` feeds `d`. With `t` off, `d` is `q` and nothing changes; with `t` on, `d` is NOT `q` and it flips.
---- done
This is a **T flip-flop**. Chain them, each one's `t` from the bits before it, and you get a counter.
